// @run
// @log 10
// @log 9
// D1120's witness. Two merged modules each export a free `self`-function called
// `area`; the entry imports ONLY `a`'s, and a dependency (`use_b.vl`) uses `b`'s
// internally. The merge's plain→mangled UFCS alias table held BOTH `area → area$mA`
// and `area → area$mB` and answered every lookup with the FIRST — and the rewrite
// walk runs dependency-first, so the dependency's call site won and the entry's
// `box(5).area()` was refused `no field 'area' on Box`: a message about a field that
// was really a wrong-alias lookup.
//
// The alias is now banked per CALL SITE (`ufcsSiteTo`, keyed by the Call node the
// merge walk already held), so each site resolves to its own module's function.
import { area, box } from "./a"
import { nine } from "./use_b"

print(box(5).area())
print(nine())
